abstract: >-
  Agentic coding benchmarks grade artifacts from single execution traces.
  Many requirements on agent-authored control systems are hyperproperties
  (predicates over sets of traces). DIPTYCH is a paired-trace grading harness
  with perturbation operators, coupling discipline, and a probe-tree cost
  model. A mutation sweep found and fixed three classes of defect in its own
  graders. In a pilot with 80 model-written controllers on two tasks, 28 of
  the 34 that pass every single-trace check on a concurrency task violate a
  requirement under paired probing, while on a congestion task built from
  RFC 9743 a single run catches every case of harm to a standard flow.
  No accuracy, AUROC, or model rankings are claimed.
